## gh issue view 8 (body)
## User story (setup)

**As a** developer on the CTA project, **I want** every commit to reference the work item it serves, **so that** any change can be traced from requirement to code to evidence without archaeology.

**Feature:** #7 · **Priority:** P0 · **Milestone:** M0 · **Owner:** shared

### Acceptance criteria

```gherkin
Scenario: Every commit on main references its work item
  Given the repository conventions in CONTRIBUTING.md
  When a developer commits a change
  Then the commit message includes "Refs #<issue>" or "Closes #<issue>"
  And the commit appears on that issue's timeline
  And pre-convention commits are listed below as explicit exceptions
```

### Deliverables

- [x] Repository created with an initial README (pre-convention commit `ae859cd`)
- [x] User-story issue form `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/user-story.yml` (commit `204eb49`)
- [x] Label taxonomy started: `user-story` added to the default set (note: personal repos have no issue custom fields, so story points/priority must live in labels)
- [ ] `CONTRIBUTING.md` defining commit, branch, and PR conventions
- [ ] Retro-attribution of pre-convention commits (recorded below)
- [ ] Follow-up (separate issue when CI exists): enforce `Refs #<issue>` on pull requests

### Pre-convention commits (retro-attributed to this story)

- `ae859cd509c077a57e1e0c46d1bf5edbde984f3f` — Initial commit (README stub), authored before conventions existed
- `204eb49810e25636461ec0e039d7e7277c1a3e89` — Add user-story issue form; predates this story's creation

### Definition of done (roadmap §9)

- `CONTRIBUTING.md` present on `main` and its own commit references this issue
- A later commit referencing `Refs #N` shows up on issue N's timeline (spot-checked)
- Conventions are consistent with the roadmap's ID scheme (`F-01`, `AS-01`, `SETUP-01`)
